# .doctrine/commands — the PROJECT'S verbs, run with `scripts/run <verb>` (one `verb = command` per line).
#
# The spine names no build tool (it is language-neutral); a pack appends its verbs at install, and
# you declare the rest. Conventional verbs, so every agent and CI job can call them without knowing
# the language: check · test · lint · fmt · build · docs. `scripts/run` refuses an undeclared verb.
#
# Examples (declare yours):
#   check = make -C build test
#   test = prove -lr t
#   docs = mkdocs build
